What:           /sys/kernel/mm/mem_boost_mode
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        E404 munch maintainers
Description:
                Root-writable, experimental launch hint. Values 0..3 are
                accepted. Zero cancels the hint; 1 is compatibility-only;
                2 and 3 prefer file reclaim in background kswapd for at most
                five seconds after each write. Value 3 does not kill tasks.
                Readback returns zero after expiry without a reset write.

                Writing try2 atomically acquires mode 2 only when no hint
                is active. An active mode returns EBUSY without extending
                its expiry. Numeric writes retain explicit override behavior.

                Applies to both legacy LRU and MGLRU. It leaves direct,
                proactive, memcg-targeted and priority-zero reclaim alone.
                Normal reclaim resumes below a file-LRU floor of 500 MiB
                on machines with at least 4 GiB RAM (400/300/200 MiB on
                smaller machines). The floor is a best-effort observation,
                not a reservation. No global VM sysctl is overwritten.

                During modes 2 and 3, automatic file readahead/read-around
                windows are capped at eight pages without changing the
                configured per-file limit. Demand reads and explicit
                readahead requests remain available. Zram writeback scans
                and submissions defer with EBUSY, including ioctl writeback;
                already submitted I/O drains before its owner returns.
                This does not cancel outstanding I/O or block swap-in,
                PAGEOUT, ordinary file writeback, or terminal rescue.

                Disabled at boot. This interface neither frees memory on
                its own nor bounds allocation latency. A userspace owner
                must measure effectiveness before enabling it in a profile.

What:           /sys/kernel/mm/mem_boost_contract
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        E404 munch maintainers
Description:
                Read-only string: e404-launch-io-v1 5000
                Identifies the above five-second reclaim/readahead/writeback
                contract, including atomic try2 admission. Userspace must not
                infer this contract from a vendor's mode filename alone.
